+++ b/features/todo-editing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+Feature: Todo Editing
+  As a user
+  I want to edit existing todo titles
+  So that I can correct or update tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Enter editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Double-click a todo label to start editing
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy milk"
+    Then "Buy milk" gains the editing class
+    And an edit input is shown containing "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Edit input is focused when editing mode is activated
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy milk"
+    Then the edit input is focused
+
+  Rule: Save edits
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on Enter
+    Given I am editing "Buy milk"
+    When I change the edit input to "Buy oat milk" and press Enter
+    Then "Buy milk" is replaced by "Buy oat milk" in the todo list
+    And the editing class is removed
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on blur
+    Given I am editing "Buy milk"
+    When I change the edit input to "Buy oat milk" and click away
+    Then "Buy milk" is replaced by "Buy oat milk" in the todo list
+
+  Scenario: Trim whitespace on save
+    Given I am editing "Buy milk"
+    When I change the edit input to "   Buy oat milk   " and press Enter
+    Then "Buy oat milk" appears in the todo list
+
+  Rule: Discard edits
+
+  Scenario: Destroy todo when edit is emptied
+    Given I am editing "Buy milk"
+    When I clear the edit input and press Enter
+    Then "Buy milk" is removed from the todo list
+
+  Scenario: Discard changes on Escape
+    Given I am editing "Buy milk" and have changed it to "Buy oat milk"
+    When I press Escape
+    Then "Buy milk" remains in the todo list unchanged
+    And the editing class is removed
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todo-persistence.feature b/features/todo-persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..92b8b4b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+Feature: Todo Persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to persist across page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: LocalStorage persistence
+
+  Scenario: Todos survive page reload
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Write specs"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then "Buy milk" and "Write specs" appear in the todo list
+
+  Scenario: Completion state persists across reload
+    Given "Buy milk" is marked as completed
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then "Buy milk" has the completed class
+
+  Scenario: Active filter route persists across reload
+    Given the URL hash is "#/active"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the URL hash remains "#/active"
+
+  Rule: LocalStorage key and format
+
+  Scenario: Todos are stored under the correct localStorage key
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    Then localStorage contains a key matching "todos-" with the todo data
+
+  Scenario: Each todo item has id, title, and completed fields
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    Then each stored todo has an id, a title, and a completed property
+
+  Rule: Editing state is not persisted
+
+  Scenario: Editing mode is not persisted
+    Given I am editing "Buy milk"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then no todo is in editing mode
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todo-routing.feature b/features/todo-routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..43a667c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+Feature: Todo Filtering and Routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter todos by status using URL routes
+  So that I can focus on active or completed items
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Route filtering
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" completed and "Write specs" active
+    When the URL hash is "#/"
+    Then both "Buy milk" and "Write specs" are displayed
+
+  Scenario: Active route shows only active todos
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" completed and "Write specs" active
+    When the URL hash changes to "#/active"
+    Then only "Write specs" is displayed
+    And "Buy milk" is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Completed route shows only completed todos
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" completed and "Write specs" active
+    When the URL hash changes to "#/completed"
+    Then only "Buy milk" is displayed
+    And "Write specs" is hidden
+
+  Rule: Selected filter link
+
+  Scenario: All filter link has selected class by default
+    Then the "All" filter link has the selected class
+
+  Scenario: Active filter link gets selected class
+    When the URL hash changes to "#/active"
+    Then the "Active" filter link has the selected class
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter link gets selected class
+    When the URL hash changes to "#/completed"
+    Then the "Completed" filter link has the selected class
+
+  Rule: Filter interaction with item updates
+
+  Scenario: Item checked while in Active filter is hidden
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Write specs"
+    And the URL hash is "#/active"
+    When I click the checkbox on "Buy milk"
+    Then "Buy milk" is hidden from the active view
+
+  Scenario: Active filter is persisted on reload
+    Given the URL hash is "#/active"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the "Active" filter link has the selected class
\ No newline at end of file
